 "circuits": [],
 "equations": [],
 "operation": [
  {
   "topic": "Internal diodes",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "Two diodes sit inside the package: the body diode, anode on the source and cathode on the drain, and a gate protection element of two zener diodes in series, back to back, from gate to source."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Gate drive",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "The threshold is 0.8 V min and 1.5 V max at 0.1 mA. On-resistance is guaranteed at two gate voltages, 4.0 V (8.0 Ω max at 10 mA) and 2.5 V (13 Ω max at 1.0 mA). With 4 V on the gate, typical on-resistance is about 5 Ω at 25 °C and 7 Ω at 125 °C, changing little with drain current up to 0.2 A."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Heat",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "Dissipation is rated 200 mW with a junction-to-ambient thermal resistance of 625 °C/W, and the junction runs from -55 to +150 °C."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Construction",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "Trench low-voltage process with a dense cell design for low on-resistance, and fast switching. The mold compound carries a UL 94V-0 flammability rating and is RoHS compliant and halogen-free. The leads are solder plated and meet MIL-STD-750 Method 2026 for solderability. Named uses are interfacing and load switching."
  }
 ],
